Packaging and Distribution\n\n### Package Structure\n\nA typical extension 
package structure:\n\n```\nmy_extension/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md\n└──
src/\n    └── my_package/\n        ├── __init__.py\n        ├── extension.py    
# Contains MyExtension class\n        └── tools.py        # Optional: Custom 
tools\n```\n\n### pyproject.toml Configuration\n\n```toml\n[project]\nname = 
"henchman-my-extension"\nversion = "1.0.0"\ndescription = "My custom extension 
for Henchman-AI"\nauthors = [{name = "Your Name", email = 
"your.email@example.com"}]\nreadme = "README.md"\nlicense = {text = 
"MIT"}\nrequires-python = ">=3.8"\ndependencies = [\n    "henchman-ai>=0.1.0",\n
# Add your extension\'s dependencies 
here\n]\n\n[project.entry-points."henchman.extensions"]\nmy_extension = 
"my_package.extension:MyExtension"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = 
["hatchling"]\nbuild-backend = "hatchling.build"\n```\n\n### Building and 
Publishing\n\n```bash\n# Install build tools\npip install build twine\n\n# Build
the package\npython -m build\n\n# Upload to PyPI\ntwine upload dist/*\n```\n\n##
Complete Example\n\nHere\'s a complete example of a simple 
extension:\n\n```python\n# my_package/extension.py\nfrom henchman.extensions 
import Extension\nfrom henchman.tools import Tool, ToolKind, ToolResult\nfrom 
henchman.cli.commands import Command, CommandContext\n\nclass GreetTool(Tool):\n
@property\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return "greet"\n    \n    
@property\n    def description(self) -> str:\n        return "Greet someone by 
name"\n    \n    @property\n    def parameters(self) -> dict[str, object]:\n    
return {\n            "type": "object",\n            "properties": {\n          
"name": {\n                    "type": "string",\n                    
"description": "Name to greet"\n                }\n            },\n            
"required": ["name"]\n        }\n    \n    @property\n    def kind(self) -> 
ToolKind:\n        return ToolKind.READ\n    \n    async def execute(self, 
**params: object) -> ToolResult:\n        name = str(params["name"])\n        
return ToolResult(content=f"Hello, {name}!")\n\nclass GreetCommand(Command):\n  
@property\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return "greet"\n    \n    
@property\n    def description(self) -> str:\n        return "Greet from 
command"\n    \n    @property\n    def usage(self) -> str:\n        return 
"/greet <name>"\n    \n    async def execute(self, ctx: CommandContext) -> 
None:\n        args = ctx.args\n        if args:\n            
ctx.console.print(f"Hello, {args[0]}!")\n        else:\n            
ctx.console.print("Hello, world!")\n\nclass MyExtension(Extension):\n    
@property\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return "greeting_extension"\n    
\n    @property\n    def version(self) -> str:\n        return "1.0.0"\n    \n  
@property\n    def description(self) -> str:\n        return "Adds greeting 
tools and commands"\n    \n    def get_tools(self):\n        return 
[GreetTool()]\n    \n    def get_commands(self):\n        return 
[GreetCommand()]\n    \n    def get_context(self):\n        return "This 
extension provides greeting functionality."\n```'})

