Extensions\n\nHenchman-AI supports extensions for adding custom functionality. 
Extensions allow third parties to add tools, commands, and additional context to
the system.\n\n## Extension Types\n\nExtensions can provide:\n\n| Type | 
Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| **Tools** | Custom tools for the agent 
to use |\n| **Commands** | Custom slash commands for the CLI |\n| **Context** | 
Additional system prompt context |\n\n**Note**: Custom provider extensions are 
not currently supported. Use the built-in provider system instead.\n\n## 
Creating Extensions\n\n### Extension Base Class\n\nCreate an extension by 
subclassing `Extension` and implementing the required 
properties:\n\n```python\nfrom henchman.extensions import Extension\nfrom 
henchman.tools import Tool, ToolKind, ToolResult\nfrom henchman.cli.commands 
import Command, CommandContext\n\nclass MyExtension(Extension):\n    """My 
custom extension."""\n    \n    @property\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        
return "my_extension"\n    \n    @property\n    def version(self) -> str:\n     
return "1.0.0"\n    \n    @property\n    def description(self) -> str:\n        
return "Adds custom tools and commands"\n    \n    def get_tools(self) -> 
list[Tool]:\n        """Return tools provided by this extension."""\n        
return [MyCustomTool()]\n    \n    def get_commands(self) -> list[Command]:\n   
"""Return slash commands provided by this extension."""\n        return 
[MyCustomCommand()]\n    \n    def get_context(self) -> str:\n        """Return 
additional system prompt context."""\n        return "Additional context for the
system prompt"\n```\n\n## Creating Extensions\n\n### Extension Base 
Class\n\n```python\nfrom henchman.extensions import Extension\n\nclass 
MyExtension(Extension):\n    """My custom extension."""\n    \n    name = 
